Stop snuffleupagus logging every nopped libxml_disable_entity_loader() call.

sp.xxe_protection.enable() replaces libxml_disable_entity_loader() with a
function that does nothing, returns true, and logs "[xxe][log] A call to
libxml_disable_entity_loader was tried and nopped" as an E_WARNING -- on every
call, whatever the argument.

On PHP 7, Symfony calls it on every XSD validation: XliffUtils::validateSchema()
and DependencyInjection's XmlFileLoader both do
`$prev = libxml_disable_entity_loader(false); ...validate...;
libxml_disable_entity_loader($prev)`, because their shouldEnableEntityLoader()
is unconditionally true below PHP 8.0. PrestaShop 8.2 on php 7.2 logged 1166 of
these in one app-suite run (laravel and wordpress none; 8.x none, Symfony skips
the call there). Nothing breaks directly, but the warning is not only noise:
PrestaShop's webservice turns any PHP warning into an error response, so a
cold translation-cache load inside an API request could fail it.

Only the log line goes. The replacement function is unchanged, so the call is
still a nop that leaves entity loading as it was. tests/test-snuffleupagus.sh
asserts the nop, the missing log line, and that
libxml_set_external_entity_loader(), the call only an attacker or a custom
loader makes, still logs. (The same hook also disables the entity loader, but
from an INI handler at startup, which does not carry into requests: this patch
neither relies on that nor changes it.)

No config knob reaches this: the log line is hard-coded in the replacement
function, and an sp.disable_function allow() only stops later rules matching,
the replacement still runs. Drop this patch when snuffleupagus stops logging
here, or when php 7.2-7.4 leave the matrix.

--- a/src/sp_disable_xxe.c
+++ b/src/sp_disable_xxe.c
@@ -1,7 +1,10 @@
 #include "php_snuffleupagus.h"
 
 PHP_FUNCTION(sp_libxml_disable_entity_loader) {
-  sp_log_warn("xxe", "A call to libxml_disable_entity_loader was tried and nopped");
+  // php-docker: nopped without a log line. On PHP 7, Symfony's XliffUtils and
+  // XmlFileLoader call this with false around every XSD validation; the call is
+  // refused either way, and the E_WARNING the log raised turns into an error
+  // response in PrestaShop's webservice.
   RETURN_TRUE;
 }
 
